  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nWellington’s Waterloo Secret\n£5.00\n\nWellington’s Waterloo Secret quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nThe most remarkable feature of all the current histories of the Battle of Waterloo is that no two descriptions of the end of the battle are the same. Why? Because the Duke of Wellington did not approve of the way the battle ended so he invented an alternative version, which has been faithfully accepted by historians, until now. But, because his version does not fit the other known facts, each historian has had to cobble together his or her own version – hence the variety.\n\nThis book concentrates of the ‘crisis’ of the battle, deduces what actually happened and adduces evidence both for the action and for the cover-up that followed.\n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre IV\n£5.00 Read more\nBugle & Sabre III\n£5.00 Read more\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
